INT. SMALL CLAIMS COURTROOM - FORMER SKATING RINK - DAY

Bleachers for gallery. Judge's bench on a rink-side Zamboni platform. Painted lines still on the floor.

JUDGE MARGUERITE VANCE, 60s, reading glasses, gavel in a fist. FELIX OYELARAN, 30s, sharp suit, stands at the plaintiff's mark. SOLVEIG HARTMANN, 40s, hands folded, at the defendant's.

VANCE
Counselor, the exhibit.

OYELARAN
Your Honor, my client's contract clearly states--

HARTMANN
Objection. Contract was never signed.

VANCE
Ms. Hartmann, let him finish.

HARTMANN
He's misstating the--

OYELARAN
I have it right here, page four--

VANCE
Both of you.

Oyelaran waves the paper. Hartmann steps toward him. Vance raises the gavel.

HARTMANN
It's a forgery, Judge. He knows it.

OYELARAN
That is a slander, and you know it.

VANCE
Order!

HARTMANN
Ask him who typed it!

OYELARAN
Ask her why she hid the original!

The gavel cracks. Once. Twice. A third time, splintering the handle.

VANCE
Sit. Down.

They sit. Silence. The old rink compressor ticks.
